---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
---
<Base title={"Underwriting"} description={"How Valley Capital Partners underwrites non-performing hotel loans."}>
<Hero eyebrow={"Underwriting"} title={"What we examine before we price a hotel loan."} lead={"We do the work before we name a figure. That is what lets us hold to the figure once we have given it."} />
<main id="main">
<section class="section"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">The hotel</p><h2>Seven questions specific to hotel collateral.</h2></div>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Area</th><th scope="col">What we need to know</th><th scope="col">Why it moves the price</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Franchise</th><td>Is the agreement in default, and does the comfort letter extend to a buyer of the loan?</td><td>A hotel that loses its flag loses much of its demand.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Improvement plan</th><td>What does the brand require, at what cost, by what date?</td><td>The cost comes ahead of any recovery on the loan.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Performance</th><td>Occupancy, average daily rate, and revenue per available room against the competitive set.</td><td>Shows whether the problem is the market, the hotel, or the operator.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Management</th><td>Who operates the hotel, on what terms, and can the agreement be ended on a transfer?</td><td>A change of manager is often the first step in a recovery.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Liabilities</th><td>Unpaid occupancy and sales taxes, payroll, vendor balances, and advance deposits.</td><td>Some of these follow the property to the next owner.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Reserves and cash</th><td>The furniture, fixtures, and equipment reserve, and who controls the accounts.</td><td>Determines what is available to keep the hotel running.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Title and ground lease</th><td>Lien priority, and the remaining term and conditions of any ground lease.</td><td>Defines what a foreclosure would deliver.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</div></section>

<section class="section alt"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">The loan</p><h2>Documents, borrower, and jurisdiction.</h2></div>
  <div class="cells">
    <div><h3>The documents</h3><p>Whether the note, mortgage, assignments, guaranties, and security filings on personal property are complete and enforceable.</p></div>
    <div><h3>The borrower</h3><p>Who controls the hotel, what they want, and whether they have the means and willingness to reach an agreement.</p></div>
    <div><h3>The jurisdiction</h3><p>How long enforcement takes in the hotel's state, and what a receiver or a bankruptcy filing would add.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Resolution</p><h2>How a hotel loan we own gets resolved.</h2>
    <p>We plan for each outcome before purchase and pursue the one that fits the hotel and the borrower.</p></div>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Outcome</th><th scope="col">When it fits</th><th scope="col">What happens</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Modification</th><td>The hotel is viable and the owner is capable and cooperative.</td><td>The loan is reset on terms the hotel can support.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Negotiated payoff</th><td>The owner can raise new capital or refinance part of the balance.</td><td>The owner pays an agreed amount and the lien is released.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Consensual transfer</th><td>The owner prefers to exit and seeks a release.</td><td>Title transfers by agreement and the hotel keeps operating.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Enforcement</th><td>No agreement can be reached.</td><td>A receiver operates the hotel while foreclosure proceeds.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Sale</th><td>Another party is better placed to own the loan or the hotel.</td><td>The loan or the hotel is sold.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</div></section>

<section class="section alt"><div class="wrap intro">
  <div><p class="eyebrow">Principles</p><h2>How we conduct ourselves with counterparties.</h2></div>
  <dl class="pillars">
    <div><dt>Price once</dt><dd>The figure does not move without a reason found in diligence.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Say no early</dt><dd>If a loan is not for us, the seller hears that within days, with the reason.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Keep it confidential</dt><dd>The existence of a discussion is confidential, as is everything in the file.</dd></div>
  </dl>
</div></section>
</main>
<Cta title={"See how we would approach your loan."} text={"Send a summary and we will tell you how we would underwrite it."} label={"Contact us"} />
</Base>
